{
  "provenance": "Operator rule (2026-09-22): OpenRouter may serve FREE models only. The openrouter upstream declares paidModelsAllowed:false, so any model whose price is unknown or non-zero is refused at dispatch (packages/core/src/compatibility.ts) \u2014 a config mistake cannot spend money. Every openrouter model id below carries the :free variant and cost 0. Ids, context windows, output ceilings, modalities and zero pricing verified live from https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models and a real completion per id on 2026-09-22. Jev (TypeSafe judge) is a separate upstream and unaffected by this rule. Operator rule (2026-09-23): Claude Code and Codex are used through their own subscriptions \u2014 Sabi installs hooks into them and never writes a provider base URL, an API key or a model override into either harness, so neither can become per-token spend through Sabi. Guarded by packages/controller/test/hooks.test.ts. Operator rule (2026-09-23): transport fallback is ON. Every configured tier is an OpenRouter `:free` model, and those are served from shared upstream pools that rate-limit the whole pool (`limit_source: upstream_provider_shared_pool` in the provider's own 429 body), so a 429 on one free model is routed to the next serving tier instead of ending the round. Fixed aliases are unaffected by design. Operator addition (2026-09-25): native Gemini via the OpenAI-compatible surface. It is NOT in the policy tiers, so default routing never selects it. It is the one upstream with paidModelsAllowed:true and must be requested by name (`sabi-gemini`). Google publishes RPM/TPM/RPD quotas per PROJECT, not per key, and no per-token price for a Free-tier key, so it cannot be proven free and is not claimed to be. Operator addition (2026-09-25): NVIDIA and Mistral upstreams added. Only models verified with a real completion against this account are listed -- codestral-latest, mistral-code-latest, nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b, nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b, nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-omni-30b-a3b-reasoning. The remaining NVIDIA catalogue entries return 404 'not found for account' or 410 Gone on this key and are deliberately absent. Both upstreams are metered and carry paidModelsAllowed:true; the openrouter free-only rule is unchanged and still enforced per-upstream. Context windows for the NVIDIA models come from the OpenRouter catalogue because NVIDIA's own /v1/models omits them.",
